1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Welcome back to ForamEcoQS. In this advanced GUI tutorial,
we verify species, manage lists, and compare EQS classifications.

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Open the synthetic abundance matrix: species are rows,
samples are columns, and every value is an integer count.

3
00:00:43,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Enable WoRMS verification and run Compare Species.
Review local matches, accepted names, synonyms, and unresolved taxa.

4
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Import the Species-and-Value CSV in Custom Lists.
Inspect its entries and document the list's source and version.

5
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Import and filter Geographic Lists to find regional references.
The displayed Adriatic records are synthetic tutorial examples.

6
00:02:40,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Reload the validated matrix, calculate the indices,
and enter the six mud percentages in sample order.

7
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:51,000
The compact colored agreement matrix reports pairwise Cohen's kappa.
Interpret the values with sample size and class distribution.

8
00:03:51,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Generate a confusion matrix. Diagonal cells are agreements;
off-diagonal cells show disagreements between EQS classes.
